WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.320
- [Instructor] We are
asked to draw the image

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.240
of triangle ABC under a dilation

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.240
whose center is P and scale factor is 1/4.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.810
So pause this video, and at least think

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.010
about how you would do this.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.780
You don't have access
to the tool that I do

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.040
where I can move this around.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.470
This is actually from the
Khan Academy exercise.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.950
But at least think about
how you would do this.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.780
Draw the image of triangle A, B, C

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.980
under a dilation whose center is P

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.113
and scale factor is 1/4.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.500
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.920
So one way to think about it is

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.530
our center of dilation is P,

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.270
and our scale factor is 1/4,

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.120
so for each of these points,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.250
however far they were from P before,

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.190
they're now going to be 1/4 as far.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.070
And one way to think about it is

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.840
is to think about it in each
of the x and the y dimensions.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.580
So for example, point A right over here,

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.700
to get from point P to point A,

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.040
you have to go one, two,
three, four to the right

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.630
and one, two, three, four down.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:05.090
So 1/4 of that in the
x and the y direction,

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.200
instead of going four to
the right and four down,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.160
1/4 of that would be one
to the right and one down

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.040
'cause one is 1/4 of four.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.230
So instead of four to the
right, we'd go one to the right,

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:19.670
and instead of four down,
we would go one down.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:22.430
So this is what point
A would get mapped to,

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.450
and now let's think about point B.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.510
In order to go from P to point B,

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:31.260
you have to go in the Y
direction up one, two, three,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.210
four, five, six, seven, eight.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.140
Well, what's 1/4 of eight?

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.460
It's two, so now we're gonna go up two,

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.280
and to go from P to B,

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.170
how much do we have to
go in the x direction?

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:49.170
Well, we have to go to the
left one, two, three, four.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.660
So instead of going four to the left,

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.460
we're now going to go 1/4 of that

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.480
or just one to the left.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.860
So instead of eight up and four left,

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.620
we're now going two up
and one to the left,

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.740
1/4 in each direction.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:05.100
And then last but not
least, to go from P to C,

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.240
it looks like we're going
one, two, three, four,

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.120
five, six, seven, eight to the left,

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.800
and one, two, three, four up.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.490
So if we take 1/4 of each of those,

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.040
instead of eight to the left,

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.240
we're now going to go two to the left.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.630
Instead of four up, we're
now going to go one up.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:25.650
And we're done.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.210
We have just created the
image of triangle ABC

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.850
under a dilation whose
center is P (chuckling)

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.803
and scale factor is 1/4.

